    "df_cellosaurus_clean[\"cosmic_xref\"]   = df_cellosaurus_clean[\"cross-references\"].apply(lambda x: extract_xref(x, \"cosmic\"))\n",
    "df_cellosaurus_clean[\"sanger_xref\"]   = df_cellosaurus_clean[\"cross-references\"].apply(lambda x: extract_xref(x, \"cell_model_passport\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Match against sample_info\n",
    "cosmic_match  = df_sample_info_cleaned[\"cosmicid\"].astype(str).isin(df_cellosaurus_clean[\"cosmic_xref\"])\n",
    "sanger_match  = df_sample_info_cleaned[\"sanger_model_id\"].isin(df_cellosaurus_clean[\"sanger_xref\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Recoverable via COSMIC :\", cosmic_match.sum())\n",
    "print(\"Recoverable via Sanger :\", sanger_match.sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "85e81a09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### INSIGHTS FROM THE DATA RECOVERY METHODS\n",
    "\n",
    "Table 1: Cellosaurus ↔ Sample_info\n",
    "(via cellosaurus_accession ↔ rrid → sanger_model_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "Dataset sizes → Cellosaurus: 152,231 rows, Sample_info: 1,840 rows (anchor)\n",
    "Initial RRID exact match → 1,812 / 1,840 = 98.48% via rrid ↔ cellosaurus_accession\n",
    "RRID null mapping → 22 / 1,840 = 1.20% have null rrid at source no accession recorded at data collection; unresolvable via RRID chain\n",
    "Deprecated/secondary accession → 2 valid-format RRIDs (CVCL_X507, CVCL_V618) absent from primary dump; secondary accession explode recovered +1 (CVCL_X507), 1 permanently lost\n",
    "Name-based fallback → safe exact name match (excluding 69 duplicate names in Cellosaurus) recovered +8 / 22 null-rrid rows\n",
    "Sanger ID mapping → sanger_model_id ↔ cell_model_passport xref recovered 1,838 / 1,840 = 99.89% supersedes RRID as primary key\n",
    "Hard floor loss → 2 / 1,840 = 0.11% both are NaN rows with no identifier; irrecoverable\n",
    "\n",
    "Resolution summary → initial loss was 28 / 1,840 = 1.52% (28 unmatched); multi-tier recovery (secondary accession +1, name fallback +8, Sanger primary key +17) resolved 26 / 28 = 92.86% of initial loss → final matching rate improved from 98.48% → 99.89% (1,838 / 1,840) with only 2 irrecoverable NaN rows (0.11%) remaining.\n",
    "\n",
    "Table 2: Sample_info ↔ DepMap Profiles\n",
    "(via depmap_id ↔ modelid)\n",
    "\n",
    "Dataset sizes → Sample_info: 1,840 rows, DepMap Profiles: 1,822 rows\n",
    "Initial depmap_id exact match → 1,749 / 1,840 = 95.05% via depmap_id ↔ modelid\n",
    "Directional loss → 91 depmap_ids in sample_info absent from profiles (4.95%); 73 modelids in profiles absent from sample_info — bidirectional gap\n",
    "Root cause → pure DepMap release version mismatch — zero format issues (identical ach- prefix, length=10, zero nulls on both sides)\n",
    "Cellosaurus xref bridge → depmap field in Cellosaurus cross-references yielded 1,893 entries; direct Cellosaurus → DepMap match = 1,768 / 1,822 = 97.04% — recovers +19 over initial join\n",
    "Residual loss → 72 / 1,840 = 3.91% — cell lines present in sample_info but absent from both depmap_profiles and cellosaurus xref; version gap irrecoverable without unified DepMap release\n",
    "\n",
    "Resolution summary → initial loss was 91 / 1,840 = 4.95% (91 unmatched from sample_info side); Cellosaurus depmap xref bridge recovered +19 records = 20.88% of initial loss resolved → final matching rate improved from 95.05% → 96.09% (1,768 / 1,840) with 72 irrecoverable records (3.91%) remaining due to release version gap.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Correction:** the \"1,838/1,840 = 99.89%\" Sanger figure above is inflated by a pandas gotcha - `.isin()` treats NaN as matching NaN, and 687/1,840 sample_info rows have a null sanger_model_id, so those were silently counted as \"matched\" against cellosaurus rows that also have a null sanger_xref. The real ceiling via Sanger alone (non-null values only) is ~1,150/1,840 (62.5%) - still the single strongest method, just not this high. See the corrected final numbers in \"INSIGHTS FROM THE HARMONIZATION\" below.\n"
   ]
  },
